Configuring Xfce4 Session:

Xfce4 can use elogind for login session tracking, runtime directories, device
access and power-management authorization when it is installed and enabled in
OpenRC. The Xfce4 PAM service includes system-session, which is populated by
the elogind package migration hook.

When building an Xfce4 package, some configuration files are installed in
/usr/share/applications, /usr/share/icons, and /usr/share/mime. In order to use
those files in your Xfce4 session, update the relevant databases as root:

    update-desktop-database &&
    update-mime-database /usr/share/mime

Starting Xfce4:

You can start Xfce4 from a display manager such as SDDM or LXDM. For a manual
xinit session, use dbus-run-session in ~/.xinitrc:

    dbus-run-session startxfce4

Ensure elogind is started before the display manager when using OpenRC:

    rc-update add elogind boot
    rc-service elogind start
